+# EPMCDME-10928: Configurable Integration URL Defaults — Implementation Plan
+
+> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.
+
+**Goal:** Fetch `GET /v1/tools/configs` at app startup and use the backend-provided URL placeholders to make integration URL defaults deployment-configurable, replacing hardcoded example strings.
+
+**Architecture:** A new `fetchToolConfigs()` method on `appInfoStore` fetches the backend config array at startup and populates `toolUrlDefaults: Record<string, string>`. A `dynUrl(credType, fallback)` helper in `settingsUIConfig.ts` returns a closure that reads from the store at render time, replacing the 15 hardcoded URL `placeholder` and `defaultUrl` values. The single consumer of `defaultUrl` (`getSettingCredsURL`) is updated to call the closure when the value is a function.
+
+**Tech Stack:** TypeScript, Valtio (proxy store), Vitest, json-server (mock)
+
+## Global Constraints
+
+- Test runner: `npx vitest run` (unit) or `npm run test`
+- Commit prefix: `EPMCDME-10928:`
+- No changes to `SettingsForm.tsx` or `CredentialFields.tsx`
+- `getDefaultUrl()` in `settings.ts` must be deleted (dead code — no callers)
+- Fallback strings must exactly match the current hardcoded values (no regressions when API fails)
+
+---
+
+### Task 1: Widen `defaultUrl` type in `settingsUI.ts`
+
+**Files:**
+- Modify: `src/types/settingsUI.ts:93`
+
+**Interfaces:**
+- Produces: `CredentialTypeConfig.defaultUrl?: string | (() => string)` — Tasks 4 and 5 depend on this
+
+- [ ] **Step 1: Change the type**
+
+In `src/types/settingsUI.ts`, replace line 93:
+
