+# Spec: EPMCDME-10928 — Configurable Integration URL Defaults (UI)
+
+## Problem
+
+Integration URL defaults (`defaultUrl`, field `placeholder`) in `settingsUIConfig.ts` are hardcoded strings. Every deployment of CodeMie shows the same example URLs (e.g. `https://jira.example.com/`) regardless of the company's actual infrastructure. The backend now serves deployment-configured values via `GET /v1/tools/configs`. The UI must read them at startup and use them in place of the hardcoded strings.
+
+---
+
+## Solution Overview
+
+1. Fetch `GET /v1/tools/configs` once at app startup (fire-and-forget). Store the parsed URL defaults in `appInfoStore.toolUrlDefaults` as a flat `Record<string, string>` keyed by UI credential type, reading the `default` field from each tool's URL field object.
+2. Replace the hardcoded `defaultUrl` values in `settingsUIConfig.ts` with `dynUrl(credType, fallback)` calls that resolve at render time from the store. Field `placeholder` strings remain hardcoded — only `defaultUrl` is made dynamic. When the store has no value (fetch failed, endpoint absent, or value empty), the original hardcoded string is returned as the fallback — no visible regression.
+3. No changes to `SettingsForm.tsx` or `CredentialFields.tsx`. The new `CredentialTypeConfig.defaultUrl` function type is handled in the one consumer that reads it (`getSettingCredsURL` in `settings.ts`).
+
+---
+
+## File-by-file Design
+
+### `src/types/settingsUI.ts`
+
+Change `defaultUrl` to accept a getter:
+
+```typescript
+// Before
+defaultUrl?: string // Defaults to 'AutoGenerated'
+
+// After
+defaultUrl?: string | (() => string)
+```
+
+`CredentialFieldConfig.placeholder` already has the same dual type — this makes `defaultUrl` consistent.
+
+---
+
+### `src/store/appInfo.ts`
+
+**New constant** — maps backend config class names to UI credential type and URL field:
+
+```typescript
+const TOOL_CONFIG_URL_MAP: Record<string, { credentialType: string; urlField: string }> = {
+  jiraconfig:           { credentialType: 'jira',          urlField: 'url'      },
+  confluenceconfig:     { credentialType: 'confluence',    urlField: 'url'      },
+  gitlabconfig:         { credentialType: 'git',           urlField: 'url'      },
+  keycloakconfig:       { credentialType: 'keycloak',      urlField: 'base_url' },
+  azuredevopsgitconfig: { credentialType: 'azuredevops',   urlField: 'url'      },
+  elasticconfig:        { credentialType: 'elastic',       urlField: 'url'      },
+  emailtoolconfig:      { credentialType: 'email',         urlField: 'url'      },
+  sonarconfig:          { credentialType: 'sonar',         urlField: 'url'      },
+  xrayconfig:           { credentialType: 'xray',          urlField: 'base_url' },
+  zephyrconfig:         { credentialType: 'zephyrscale',   urlField: 'url'      },
+  servicenowconfig:     { credentialType: 'servicenow',    urlField: 'url'      },
+  reportportalconfig:   { credentialType: 'reportportal',  urlField: 'url'      },
+  kubernetesconfig:     { credentialType: 'kubernetes',    urlField: 'url'      },
+  sharepointconfig:     { credentialType: 'sharepoint',    urlField: 'url'      },
+  xwikiconfig:          { credentialType: 'xwiki',         urlField: 'url'      },
+}
+```
+
+`githubconfig` is intentionally excluded — the `git` UI type represents GitLab. `keycloak` and `xray` use `base_url` as the backend field name; all others use `url`.
+
+**New store members** added to `AppInfoStoreType` and `appInfoStore`:
+
+```typescript
+// Interface
+toolUrlDefaults: Record<string, string>
+fetchToolConfigs: () => Promise<void>
+
+// Implementation
+toolUrlDefaults: {},
+
+async fetchToolConfigs() {
+  try {
+    const response = await api.get('v1/tools/configs')
+    const data: Array<Record<string, Record<string, unknown>>> = await response.json()
+    const defaults: Record<string, string> = {}
+
+    for (const entry of data) {
+      const [configKey, configVal] = Object.entries(entry)[0]
+      const mapping = TOOL_CONFIG_URL_MAP[configKey.toLowerCase()]
+      if (!mapping) continue
+      const field = configVal[mapping.urlField] as Record<string, unknown> | undefined
+      const defaultVal = field?.default
+      if (typeof defaultVal === 'string' && defaultVal) {
+        defaults[mapping.credentialType] = defaultVal
+      }
+    }
+
+    this.toolUrlDefaults = defaults
+  } catch {
+    // Non-fatal — fallback values in settingsUIConfig.ts remain in effect
+  }
+},
+```
+
+Errors are intentionally swallowed. An empty `toolUrlDefaults` means `dynUrl()` falls back to the hardcoded string for every credential type.
+
+---
+
+### `src/hooks/appLevel/useInitialDataFetch.tsx`
+
+Add one fire-and-forget call alongside the existing pattern (no `await`):
+
+```typescript
+appInfoStore.fetchToolConfigs()
+```
+
+Placed after `fetchCustomerConfig()` which is the last awaited call, consistent with the other non-blocking fetches (`getLLMModels`, `getEmbeddingsModels`, etc.).
+
+---
+
+### `src/utils/settingsUIConfig.ts`
+
+**New helper** at the top of the file (after imports):
+
+```typescript
+import { appInfoStore } from '@/store/appInfo'
+
+const dynUrl = (credType: string, fallback: string): (() => string) =>
+  () => appInfoStore.toolUrlDefaults[credType] || fallback
+```
+
+**Updated `CREDENTIAL_UI_MAPPING` entries** — the 15 credential types that have backend-configurable URLs get their `defaultUrl` replaced with a `dynUrl()` call. Field `placeholder` strings are **not changed** — they remain hardcoded.
+
+| Credential type | `defaultUrl` fallback |
+|---|---|
+| `jira` | `https://jira.example.com/` |
+| `confluence` | `http://confluence.example.com/` |
+| `git` | `https://gitlab.example.com` |
+| `keycloak` | `https://keycloak.example.com/auth` |
+| `azuredevops` | `https://dev.azure.com` |
+| `elastic` | `https://localhost:9200` |
+| `email` | `smtp.office365.com:587` |
+| `sonar` | `http://localhost:9000` |
+| `xray` | `https://xray.cloud.getxray.app` |
+| `zephyrscale` | `https://api.zephyrscale.smartbear.com/v2` |
+| `servicenow` | `https://dev000000.service-now.com/` |
+| `reportportal` | `https://reportportal.example.com/` |
+| `kubernetes` | `https://kubernetes.default.svc` (added — previously no `defaultUrl`) |
+| `sharepoint` | `https://yourtenant.sharepoint.com` |
+| `xwiki` | `https://wiki.example.com` |
+
+Note: `kubernetes` form field is `kubernetes_url` (not `url`) — the backend `urlField` used for lookup is still `url`; the UI `placeholder` on `kubernetes_url` is unchanged.
+
+All other `defaultUrl` entries (those not in the 15-entry map above) remain unchanged.
+
+---
+
+### `src/utils/settings.ts`
+
+`getSettingCredsURL()` must resolve a `defaultUrl` that may now be a getter:
+
+```typescript
+export const getSettingCredsURL = (
+  credentialValues: SettingCredentialValue[],
+  credentialType: string
+): string => {
+  const credConfig = CREDENTIAL_UI_MAPPING[credentialType]
+  const rawDefault = credConfig?.defaultUrl ?? CREDENTIAL_DEFAULTS.defaultUrl
+  const defaultUrl = typeof rawDefault === 'function' ? rawDefault() : rawDefault
+  const urlObj = credentialValues.find((cv) => cv.key === 'url')
+  return (urlObj?.value as string) || defaultUrl
+}
+```
+
+`getDefaultUrl()` is exported but has no callers outside `settings.ts` — delete it.
+
+---
+
+### `mock-server/routes.json`
+
+Add the route mapping:
+
+```json
+"/v1/tools/configs": "/tools_configs"
+```
+
+---
+
+### `mock-server/db.json`
+
+Add a `tools_configs` array that mirrors the real API format. Each entry is a single-key object with the config class name as the key. Each URL field object uses a `default` key for the deployment URL. The fixture includes all 15 mapped configs plus `githubconfig` (unmapped) to verify the parser skips unknowns gracefully.
+
+---
+
+## Data Flow
+
+```
+App startup
+  └── useInitialDataFetch
+        └── appInfoStore.fetchToolConfigs()   [fire-and-forget]
+              └── GET /v1/tools/configs
+                    └── parse field.default → toolUrlDefaults: { jira: 'https://...', ... }
+
+Settings page render
+  └── CREDENTIAL_UI_MAPPING.jira.defaultUrl()
+        └── dynUrl('jira', 'https://jira.example.com/')()
+              └── appInfoStore.toolUrlDefaults['jira'] || 'https://jira.example.com/'
+```
+
+---
+
+## Fallback / Error Behaviour
+
+| Scenario | Result |
+|---|---|
+| `fetchToolConfigs` throws (network, 5xx) | `toolUrlDefaults` stays `{}` — all `dynUrl()` calls return the hardcoded fallback |
+| Endpoint returns empty array | Same — `toolUrlDefaults` stays `{}` |
+| Entry present but `placeholder` is `""` | Empty string is falsy — `dynUrl()` returns the fallback |
+| Settings page renders before fetch completes | `toolUrlDefaults` is `{}` at that moment — fallback shown. No re-render wiring needed: the settings page is not visible in the render cycle before startup completes |
+
+---
+
+## Out of Scope
+
+- `github` credential type — backend uses `DEFAULT_GITHUB_TOOL_URL` but the `git` UI type represents GitLab; no `githubconfig` mapping in the UI.
+- `keycloak` and `xray` backend use `base_url`; the UI form field is `url`. The `TOOL_CONFIG_URL_MAP` lookup uses the backend field name; the `settingsUIConfig.ts` update targets the UI field name — they are intentionally different.
+- Re-rendering when `toolUrlDefaults` changes after initial load. The store fetch is fire-and-forget and completes before users can navigate to the settings page.
+- No new unit tests for `settingsUIConfig.ts` as it is a config module with no testable logic beyond the existing `settings.ts` tests.
